<title>USA: Arden Group Q3 shr $1.06 vs $1.37.</title>
<headline>Arden Group Q3 shr $1.06 vs $1.37.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Third quarter</p>
<p>						     1996/a	 1995/a</p>
<p> Sales					 $62,891,000  $60,968,000</p>
<p> Operating income			  1,585,000/b    2,131,000</p>
<p>Interest, dividend and other income</p>
<p>  (expense), net			     156,000/c	558,000</p>
<p>Unrealized gain on marketable securities</p>
<p>						     202,000	296,000</p>
<p> Income before income taxes		1,943,000    2,985,000</p>
<p> Income-tax provision			  769,000    1,184,000</p>
<p> Net income				    1,174,000    1,801,000</p>
<p> Net income per common share		    1.06	   1.37</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares</p>
<p>  outstanding				  1,108,999    1,314,112</p>
<p>								 39 weeks</p>
<p>						    1996/a	  1995/a</p>
<p> Sales				     $186,371,000  $181,226,000</p>
<p> Operating income			 3,717,000/b     6,234,000</p>
<p>Interest, dividend and other income</p>
<p>  (expense), net			    474,000/c     1,321,000</p>
<p>Unrealized gain (loss) on marketable</p>
<p>  securities				  (548,000)     1,484,000</p>
<p> Income before income taxes	     3,643,000     9,039,000</p>
<p> Income-tax provision		     1,440,000     3,567,000</p>
<p> Net income				   2,203,000     5,472,000</p>
<p> Net income per common share		   1.97	    4.16</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares</p>
<p>  outstanding				 1,117,303     1,314,112</p>
<p>/a  Third-quarter 1996 ended on Sept. 28, 1996, and third-quarter 1995 ended on Sept. 30, 1995. /b  The decrease in 1996 is due primarily to the opening of a new store in January 1996, increased depreciation expense in 1996 compared with 1995 levels and the recognition of certain union- benefit credits in 1995 that were nonrecurring in 1996. /c  Includes $294,000 and $826,000 less interest and dividend income in the third quarter and 39 weeks of 1996, respectively, compared with the same periods in 1995.  Also includes realized gains (losses) on sale of marketable securities ($50,000) in the third quarter of 1996, compared with $66,000 in the third quarter of 1995, and ($70,000) in the 39 weeks of 1996, compared with ($297,000) in the 39 weeks of 1995.</p>
